  "reason": "The control text and the AWS Config rule it quotes say a plan \"has a backup rule that satisfies\" the frequency and 35-day retention, an at-least-one quantifier. The original proposal kept that predicate but carried a non-enum category, an invented \"enabled rule\" notion, no operator-policy provenance and placeholder prose. The revised spec fixes those and binds the frequency to an explicit operator declaration, never a default. The original proposal is kept here unchanged.",
  "recorded": "2026-10-13"
